mppgo
=====

This library reads Microsoft Project files in Go.

The MPP file format is proprietary and undocumented. Microsoft has never
published a specification for it. Everything this library knows about the
binary layout of an MPP file — the meaning of the FixedMeta/FixedData and
VarMeta/Var2Data block structures, the Props key values, the calendar data
encoding, the date/time epoch, and the stream obfuscation scheme — derives
from the reverse engineering work of the MPXJ project:

    MPXJ - https://github.com/joniles/mpxj
    Copyright (c) Packwood Software
    Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 or later

MPXJ's Java source was read as the reference for understanding the format.
No MPXJ source code was copied into this project; the Go implementation here
was written independently against that understanding. Nonetheless, the
format knowledge that makes this library possible is MPXJ's contribution,
and that debt is acknowledged here explicitly.

If you need broad, production-grade Microsoft Project support today —
including MPP8/9/12, Primavera, Asta, Planner and many other formats — use
MPXJ. It is mature, actively maintained, and available for Java, .NET,
Python and Ruby.
